ers, along with his brother, has been slain in conflict.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.54,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-47-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6037008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bcabaab7d35df4896e19a2461c0185aae6b5e5ddb0bf00efebd77d9dc75e3296","compact":"13b038c640b9b8c4453148c2bcdcf3652ffb9055c41f6414ba3172b7168dfd48","nasal":"13b038c640b9b8c4453148c2bcdcf3652ffb9055c41f6414ba3172b7168dfd48"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-37-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":37,"verse":9,"english":"Then methyl's daughter, her fear gone off with her anxiety, and herself losing all support, Sītādaughter to methyl-decked out in all ornaments, shall seek me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-47-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6037009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff8cd854e3dfbaecc62744cfefb825eb595e2fc757d14a58428da8378685dfbe","compact":"61f2456e216e527bae656842c583ed98f0c0795b735103c8d2169eed89da6ce9","nasal":"b31083929e4c3afeb04b2d54e9853551c9cd2107f58c0204563e7d69d9fc25f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-37-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":37,"verse":10,"english":"And today beholding Rāma with Lakşmaņa, come under the away of Time, she, finding no other way, shall desist from her present course. And seeing no other resource, that one of expansive eyes shall of herself seek me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-47-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6037010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a9cd77a0e21a8324a16f5a7e850989636aac5b73c21e9d8df4270206c631af3","compact":"8a0150662fe96c5d93fa1d459402aa3bcb2b551a202539ba4374bc665a2e8731","nasal":"8a0150662fe96